===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|with {{m|en|on}}, {{q|archaic}} {{m|en|for}}}} To officially charge someone in a [[court of law]].
#: {{ux|en|He was '''arraigned''' in Washington, D.C., on the 25th of that month on charges of treason.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Ben Protess; Jonah E. Bromwich; William K. Rashbaum; Kate Christobek; Nate Schweber|title=Trump Is Indicted, Becoming First Ex-President to Face Criminal Charges|work=The New York Times|date=2023-03-30|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/03/30/nyregion/trump-indictment-hush-money-charges.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=He will then be '''arraigned''', at which point the specific charges will be unsealed.}}
# To [[call to account]], or accuse, before the [[bar]] of reason, taste, or any other [[tribunal]].
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aeneis|passage=They will not dare to '''arraign''' you for want of knowledge.}}
#* {{RQ:Isaac Taylor Saturday Evening|passage=It is not arrogance, but timidity, of which the Christian body should now be '''arraigned''' by the world.}}

